  "notes": "Outlaw-leaning arena country, built by a rock producer who tracks bands live with minimal click. The entry hands the engine an explicit instruction and this model is mostly that instruction: drums are cut \"with musicians playing together in one room without headphones, baffles for separation, drums the only isolated source, minimal click tracks and minimal overdubs so the band can 'go with their gut.' Model loose timing (tempo drift across the song is *correct* here), roomy overheads, and fills that break the pattern.\" So `quantizeStrength` is the lowest in this batch at 0.6, the jitter runs to double digits, and the fill grid is short and switchy rather than pinned to the 8-bar turnaround. The bass is the second real delta: \"live bass with overdrive, following the guitar riff rather than the kick; register mid-low and audible as a melodic voice,\" which is `independent_riff` with root-following well below the genre's boom-chick and a register that reaches higher than any other bass in this batch. Harmony is \"I–♭VII–IV, I–IV–V, and i–VI–III–VII on the dark cuts; extended vamps on a single chord are in-palette\" — the vamp weight carries that last claim. Melody is \"baritone, drawled, back-phrased, with spoken interjections; chorus melodies are anthemic but rhythmically loose against the band.\" ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: high-medium); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the jitter values, the velocity tiers and the counter ratio.",
